id: pm-vcs-3dxi
title: Enable the gated pm-github issue sync and remove the braces chain
description: "Adopt the pinned reusable issue-sync caller and preserve the existing CI workflow_dispatch trigger. Related adoption task: pm-github-aiok. Refresh the exact published pm-ops pin and remove unused fast-glob, addressing existing dependency issue pm-vcs-qfku. Record the Node 22 retention flake separately; regenerate the self-host bundle after tracker/changelog writes and staged new files, commit, then verify at HEAD. Never execute the sync or change repository settings."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: changed
created_at: "2026-10-15T07:41:09.216Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T12:26:55.056Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-15T07:42:22.476Z",codex-agent,"Baseline npm ls braces fast-glob micromatch shows fast-glob 3.3.3 -> micromatch 4.0.8 -> braces 3.0.3, also the optional peer of pm-ops 2026.10.6. Production-only tree is empty. The production duplication launcher and raw coverage inventory already use node:fs globSync; fast-glob has no direct code import. Refresh pm-ops to latest published 2026.10.14 and remove the direct peer. CI already has workflow_dispatch; use the prescribed pm-github 2026.10.14 fallback pending release and repin. No sync execution or repository settings changes."
  "2026-10-15T07:49:21.519Z",codex-agent,"Related work: pm-vcs-qfku tracks the removed vulnerable dependency chain; pm-vcs-1bcq records the reproduced Node 22 GC measurement race and one-flag deterministic test fix with flag-only revert and held-corpus negative controls. The fallback reusable workflow predates caller-changelog regeneration and CI dispatch from pm-github PR 122; the later 2026.10.15 repin remains an operational dependency."
  "2026-10-15T07:49:51.061Z",codex-agent,"PM-linked validation passes: npm run typecheck; npm run duplicates (65 sources, 0 clone pairs); retained-corpus focused test 1/1. The one-flag measurement fix has a flag-removal failing revert and a genuinely retained corpus failing control. Preparing the committed self-host snapshot before full isolated npm and Bun release gates. Both workflow/dependency changes preserve runtime code and quality thresholds."
  "2026-10-15T08:43:47.843Z",codex-agent,The first isolated npm attempt caught the pre-existing copied prepare launcher no longer matching the newly published pm-ops 2026.10.14 template; stopped that failed attempt and preserved its output. Refreshed only from the installed published template. Its new artifact guard skips package resolution and merge-driver configuration during npm pack/publish. Added two real-checkout regressions covering both commands with pinned and stale pm-ops. The complete focused launcher suite passes 10/10. Revert proof and final committed-head full gates follow; the npm/Bun thresholds remain unchanged.
  "2026-10-15T08:45:36.516Z",codex-agent,"Launcher behavioural revert proof: retain both new regression tests and restore ONLY scripts/prepare-merge-driver.ts from the pre-upgrade source. Both npm pack and npm publish scenarios fail (0/2) on a stale package export before the intended skip. Restoring the exact published pm-ops 2026.10.14 template passes the full launcher suite 10/10 with zero skips. The real Git-config invariants and dependency-resolution assertions remain intact. No unmerged template was copied."
  "2026-10-15T09:47:24.296Z",codex-agent,"Final committed-source gates at 90ba1c0 PASS: isolated Node 26.7.0 npm run release:check and bun run release:check each pass 1536/1536 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations. All 65 authored sources meet unchanged per-file 100% statements/lines/branches/functions: 22488/22488 statements and lines, 759/759 functions, 6532/6532 branches. The 355-declaration docstring gate, zero-duplication gate, native TOON, installed-CLI stat-cache strace, committed self-host equality, production audit, identity audit, package dry-run, changelog and release date/provenance checks all pass. Built and packed Node/Bun consumers pass within the suites. The copied launcher mismatch was introduced by upgrading pm-ops without refreshing its copy; it was corrected with the exact published template, two behavioral regressions, 0/2 old-launcher revert failures and 10/10 restored passes. The target launcher alone also has 100% coverage in all four dimensions. No SDK pin, thresholds or existing histories were changed. Final tracker receipts and claim releases will regenerate the snapshot before final HEAD checks."
  "2026-10-15T09:49:03.520Z",codex-agent,"Receipt clarification: the old-launcher revert had zero passing and two failing new artifact regressions; the restored launcher suite had ten passing and zero failing tests. Existing history records were preserved byte-for-byte; tracker changes append new records. All three rollout-related claims are released while the items remain in progress for orchestrator verification."
